            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "id": 98775,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "For example:\n\n```\n> object <- hashtab()\n> object$key <- 42\nError in numhash(x) : not a proper hash table object\n> object\nError in numhash(x) : not a proper hash table object\n```\n\nFrom the documentation of `?hashtab`, it looks like access (or assignment) via `$` and `$<-` isn't supported, but it seems worth either:\n\n1. Supporting access and assignment via `$` for hash tables (perhaps using the accessed value as a string?)\n\n2. Explicitly disallowing access / assignment through `$`, and preventing `$<-` from \"corrupting\" the hashtab object.\n\nSomewhat relatedly, the documentation also states fairly explicitly:\n\n> As an experimental feature, the element operator [[ can also be used get or set hash table entries, and length can be used to obtain the number of entries. It is not yet clear whether this is a good idea.\n\nHas a decision been made as to whether the interface can be considered stable?\n\n---\n\n```\n> sessionInfo()\nR version 4.2.0 (2022-04-22)\nPlatform: aarch64-apple-darwin21.3.0 (64-bit)\nRunning under: macOS Monterey 12.4\n```",
            "bug_id": 18353,
            "count": 0,
            "creation_time": "2022-06-07T22:10:14Z"
          },
          {
