            "bug_id": 18353,
            "text": "Created attachment 3546\nAlso disallow `[` and `[<-`",
            "count": 2,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": 3546,
            "id": 102225,
            "time": "2025-09-12T13:39:57Z",
            "is_private": false
          },
          {
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 3,
            "text": "For me, direct assignment like this (especially a key with no value) doesn't make sense.  The `sethash()` function provides access and ensures that it is done properly. \n\n```\n> object <- hashtab()\n> sethash(object, \"1\", 2)\n> object\n<hashtable 0x1248c5760: count = 1, type = \"identical\">\n> gethash(object, \"1\")\n[1] 2\n\n\n```\n\nIf the method is added, I think it should be to signal an error and then preventing corruption of the hash table.",
            "bug_id": 18353,
            "creator": "elin.waring",
            "creation_time": "2025-09-13T19:03:55Z",
